{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00709",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 2.68,
      "end_seconds": 13.76,
      "duration_seconds": 11.08,
      "text": "Hi, are you Dan? Take a seat, the doctor's running five minutes behind. I've just updated your student details. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.04,
      "end_seconds": 26.37,
      "duration_seconds": 9.33,
      "text": "Cool. Can we hurry it up? I've got a lecture at two and I'm already behind. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.93,
      "end_seconds": 37.32,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "Hello Dan, I'm Dr Okafor. I'll be quick but thorough. What's brought you in? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.82,
      "end_seconds": 52.94,
      "duration_seconds": 12.12,
      "text": "I'm knackered. I had a bad flu in October, and I've never really got over it. It's been six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.22,
      "end_seconds": 59.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "What does knackered feel like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.78,
      "end_seconds": 73.23,
      "duration_seconds": 10.45,
      "text": "Like my battery's at ten percent. I sleep nine hours and wake up tired. I can't concentrate in lectures."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.45,
      "end_seconds": 78.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Any other symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.04,
      "end_seconds": 89.49,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "My throat's been sore on and off, and my glands feel lumpy, here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.3,
      "end_seconds": 97.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Any fever, night sweats, or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.46,
      "end_seconds": 104.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "No fever. I'd have noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.31,
      "end_seconds": 113.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "How's your university life? Sleep, stress, workload? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.43,
      "end_seconds": 127.51,
      "duration_seconds": 10.08,
      "text": "I'm doing a double module and a part-time job at the bar. So, not much downtime. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.72,
      "end_seconds": 140.36,
      "duration_seconds": 8.64,
      "text": "That's a lot. Have you been in contact with anyone with glandular fever? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.69,
      "end_seconds": 148.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "My housemate had it last month. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.53,
      "end_seconds": 155.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "That's interesting, and relevant. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.96,
      "end_seconds": 164.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Do you think I've got it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.2,
      "end_seconds": 183.28,
      "duration_seconds": 16.08,
      "text": "I can't rule out glandular fever, given your housemate, the sore throat, the tender glands, and fatigue after a viral illness, though it could also be a slow recovery from the flu."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.41,
      "end_seconds": 190.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Can you test for it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.62,
      "end_seconds": 204.5,
      "duration_seconds": 10.88,
      "text": "Yes, I'd like to arrange a blood test, to check for the glandular fever virus and your blood count."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 208.04,
      "end_seconds": 215.27,
      "duration_seconds": 7.23,
      "text": "I can book that in for you now, Dan, at the front desk. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.22,
      "end_seconds": 222.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Fine. Does it hurt? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 225.41,
      "end_seconds": 228.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Just a quick scratch. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.15,
      "end_seconds": 241.71,
      "duration_seconds": 8.56,
      "text": "In the meantime, no contact sports, in case your spleen is enlarged, and avoid alcohol until we know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.62,
      "end_seconds": 249.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "No alcohol, that'll be hard in Freshers' week. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.72,
      "end_seconds": 257.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "It's not Freshers' week, Dan. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.95,
      "end_seconds": 264.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Ha, no. But the bar job. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.77,
      "end_seconds": 277.76,
      "duration_seconds": 9.99,
      "text": "Maybe ask for shifts that don't involve lifting crates, too. Rest when you can, and eat regularly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.85,
      "end_seconds": 283.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.42,
      "end_seconds": 298.24,
      "duration_seconds": 10.82,
      "text": "If you get severe tummy pain on the left side, or a high fever, or difficulty swallowing, come in the same day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.34,
      "end_seconds": 306.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Okay, okay. Thanks, doc. ~"
    }
  ]
}
